Read the section below and return three things.

1. `summary` — one or two sentences saying what this section is about. Written for a person, not for matching.

2. `answers` — the questions a real user would ask that THIS SECTION can answer. This is the important field, so give it the most care:
   - Write them the way a user would actually type them, not the way the document phrases them. Users write "how much are the fees for grade 5", not "Tuition Fee Schedule, Elementary".
   - Cover the section's distinct facts. If it holds four unrelated details, write at least one question per detail rather than four rewordings of the same one.
   - Include the obvious short forms people really send: "fees?", "uniform?", "when does term start".
{% if languages %}
   - Write each question in {{ languages }}. Users ask in whichever they prefer, and a question only matches if the same language is represented.
{% endif %}
   - Between {{ min_questions }} and {{ max_questions }} questions.
   - Only questions this section genuinely answers. A question you invent that the text does not cover will make the assistant accept subjects it cannot help with.

